const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文研究2010年5月6日电子市场遭遇大规模、短暂卖压时，日内中介活动如何表现。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“The Flash Crash: High-Frequency Trading in an Electronic Market” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/jofi.12498",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2017) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2017) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源使用该事件日和此前三日 E-mini 的审计轨迹逐笔数据，并以活跃的非指定日内中介者为分类对象。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “The Flash Crash: High-Frequency Trading in an Electronic Market”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/jofi.12498",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2017) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2017) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"必须保留审计轨迹成交、参与者分类、合约身份、事件时钟、前后比较窗口和市场状态。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “The Flash Crash: High-Frequency Trading in an Electronic Market”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/jofi.12498",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2017) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2017) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"摘要只描述特定事件和分类下的中介交易模式；它不把高频交易当成单一行为类型，也不对所有极端波动作因果归因。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “The Flash Crash: High-Frequency Trading in an Electronic Market”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/jofi.12498",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2017) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2017) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"确认事件时间轴、品种和参与者分类版本，区分订单、成交和头寸字段，并保存用于比较的前期窗口。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “The Flash Crash: High-Frequency Trading in an Electronic Market”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/jofi.12498",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2017) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2017) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 The Journal of Finance (2017)。单一压力事件、单一期货合约和受限审计数据不能由公开分钟行情替代，也不能推出一般性市场质量判断。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites The Journal of Finance (2017) for “The Flash Crash: High-Frequency Trading in an Electronic Market”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.1111/jofi.12498",label:{zh:"The Journal of Finance (2017) · 来源说明",en:"The Journal of Finance (2017) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“The Flash Crash: High-Frequency Trading in an Electronic Market”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。单一压力事件、单一期货合约和受限审计数据不能由公开分钟行情替代，也不能推出一般性市场质量判断。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “The Flash Crash: High-Frequency Trading in an Electronic Market”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
